body:
DONE V32. Host-tested only: no phone, no publish.

Test command (from the work-tree root):
  bash gpu/hwcodec/shim/test_v32/run_tests.sh
Last line:
  N2TEST V32 PASS 12705/12705
Full output of that run:
  == build: asan -> V32DIRECTRESULT 2386/2386, V32RESULT 10319/10319
  == build: o2   -> V32DIRECTRESULT 2386/2386, V32RESULT 10319/10319
  == build: tsan -> V32DIRECTRESULT 2386/2386, V32RESULT 10293/10293
  N2TEST V32 PASS 12705/12705
(ASan+UBSan -O1, plain -O2, TSan -O1; ~25 s; at most two compiler jobs; everything under /tmp/n2hw-v32.)

What the acceptance test really does: a REAL ARM shared object (gpu/hwcodec/shim/test_v32/arm/t_v32_guest.c, no libc, clang --target=armv7a-linux-androideabi -marm -march=armv8-a -mfloat-abi=soft -fPIC -shared -nostdlib) is loaded by V03s real loader and executed by V02s real interpreter:
  - 8 threads x 100000 increments under a never-pthread_mutex_init-ed (.bss, all-zero) mutex -> exactly 800000;
  - producer/consumer mutex+cond, ring 8, 2000 items, 4 consumers, sums equal;
  - sem ping-pong 2x5000 + sem_getvalue + EBUSY on re-init + EAGAIN on empty trywait;
  - pthread_once from 8 threads on a zero-initialised control (runs once; re-entrant call returns EDEADLK);
  - rwlock 4 readers / 2 writers, no torn read;
  - lifecycle: join/exit values, detach via attr and via pthread_detach (both EINVAL in join while alive), kill, setname_np+prctl(PR_GET_NAME), gettid/gettid_np, self/equal;
  - sched/affinity (8 CPUs, set accepted), sched_yield, usleep, sigaction/sigemptyset/signal (recorded, never delivered), __register_atfork, EBUSY/ETIMEDOUT/EDEADLK/EPERM paths;
  - pthread_exit on the initial thread -> cpu stops with N2A32_STOP_REQUEST, host process survives, marker after the call never written;
  - failure propagation: a thread with an unmapped start address records N2A32_STOP_FAULT in the first-failure slot and sets stop_request on every other live cpu (initial thread included); three threads blocked in sem_wait are released and all stop with N2A32_STOP_REQUEST; no extra failure recorded; no thread left running.
The second binary (t_direct) drives n2shim_thread[] with a fake cpu: all 50 D01 names resolve, no duplicate name, NULL/zero/out-of-range ids return the documented errno, attr/sched-param/policy round trips, cpuset bit pattern, signal recording, side-table create/destroy/kind-clash, failure slot.

TSan: clean (no data races) after fixing a race in MY TEST (worker threads shared the ck() counter; they now use per-thread failure slots). One deliberate exception: the TSan build runs with --no-fault and skips the two entries that fault inside the guest, because V02s fault handler siglongjmps out of a SIGSEGV handler and TSan aborts with "can not find longjmp buf". Everything else, including all thread/mutex/cond/sem/once/rwlock work, runs under TSan.

Extra check: bash gpu/hwcodec/shim/test_v32/compile_ios.sh -> N2TEST V32-IOS PASS 1/1 (arm64-apple-ios16.5, compile only). Darwin paths: no gettid (pthread_self), pthread_setname_np(name) for self, no pthread_mutex_timedlock/pthread_rwlock_timed*lock (trylock+poll fallback).

Integration (n2-iv/n2-ip): n2elf_set_add_shims(set, n2shim_thread) before n2elf_link; V34s data table still needed for __stack_chk_guard/stderr. Join guest threads before n2a32_mem_destroy; n2shim_thread_request_stop() for teardown; n2shim_thread_failure() after any n2a32_call that did not return N2A32_STOP_RETURN (n2shim_thread_note_stop(c) records the daemons own call in the same slot). The shim never prints, never allocates host heap, never aborts.

Not done / open (full list in gpu/hwcodec/shim/test_v32/STATUS.md):
  1. no phone run, no arm64 runtime test, not linked into n2vcodecd;
  2. R1 F8: V02 still reads n2a32_cpu::stop_request with a plain volatile load (n2a32_core.c:468) while V32 stores atomically from another host thread. One-line V02 fix proposed (__atomic_load_n ACQUIRE). My TSan run is clean because the propagation test orders the pair through my locks, but the contract is not fully atomic until V02 changes that line;
  3. guest threads that are never joined/never detached stay as host-thread records (bionic zombies); undestroyed static objects stay in the side table (limits 128 threads / 512 objects / 32 pooled 1 MiB stacks; EAGAIN/ENOMEM when exhausted);
  4. no cancellation, real signal delivery, atfork handlers, TLS, pshared semaphores, pthread_attr_setstacksize, PTHREAD_RECURSIVE_MUTEX_INITIALIZER_NP statics; timed waits use host CLOCK_REALTIME;
  5. __register_atfork is in V32 per TASK while D01s census assigned it to V34 (question to hw-lead, unanswered; duplicate is mechanically harmless);
  6. the vendor libraries have not been run through the shim yet, so their real thread/object counts are unmeasured.

Files (committed cd04fc1, only mine): gpu/hwcodec/shim/n2shim_thread.c, gpu/hwcodec/shim/n2shim_thread.h, gpu/hwcodec/shim/test_v32/{run_tests.sh,compile_ios.sh,t_direct.c,t_e2e.c,arm/t_v32_guest.c,STATUS.md}, gpu/hwcodec/dsh-state/workers/V32/STATUS.md.
Staying available for review findings and integration questions.
